>>
Rule 1 (input must be 2D or 3D to avoid shape indexing errors and 1D inputs)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 3
>>
Rule 2 (when tracking running stats, use 3D input so C is inferred from size(1))
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 then ndim(v_2) = 3
>>
Rule 3 (valid non-empty channel and length dimensions for 3D input)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 then shape(v_1, 1) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 4 (2D inputs must have C equal to L to match lazy num_features inference from size(1))
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 7 (eps must be positive)
{v_1 : float} |= v_1 > 0
>>
Rule 8 (momentum must be within [0, 1))
{v_1 : float} |= v_1 ≥ 0 ∧ v_1 < 1
